1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:06,784
Millions of families save in an arisan: everyone pays in each month, and one person takes the whole pot.

2
00:00:06,784 --> 00:00:10,575
But someone has to hold the cash, and turns slip.

3
00:00:10,575 --> 00:00:14,050
What if a Solana program held the pot instead?

4
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:19,850
This is Arisan, spelled A. R. I. S. A. N.

5
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:25,350
Here it is on a Solana Seeker, installed from our Android APK.

6
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:30,600
It connects through Mobile Wallet Adapter, and Seed Vault approves.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,392
Now a whole circle with three wallets.

8
00:00:34,392 --> 00:00:40,600
Ana creates it: three seats, zero point one SOL a round, and a zero point one SOL stake.

9
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:45,385
She takes her seat and puts in her stake.

10
00:00:45,685 --> 00:00:56,635
Boo-dee and Chitra join with the invite code, and stake from their own wallets.

11
00:00:56,935 --> 00:01:01,435
The circle can only start once every seat is taken and staked.

12
00:01:01,735 --> 00:01:07,835
Round one: everyone pays zero point one SOL with one tap.

13
00:01:08,135 --> 00:01:13,435
Here is a payment from our live dev-net circle, on Solana Explorer.

14
00:01:13,735 --> 00:01:17,080
Then anyone can run the draw: commit, then draw.

15
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:21,035
A block hash nobody knew at commit time picks the winner.

16
00:01:21,335 --> 00:01:28,735
The vault pays the whole pot in the same transaction.

17
00:01:29,035 --> 00:01:33,333
Each seat wins exactly once.

18
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:40,701
Round two goes to Chitra, and round three to Boo-dee.

19
00:01:41,001 --> 00:01:45,096
At the end, every stake comes back.

20
00:01:45,096 --> 00:01:47,826
No lender, no interest.

21
00:01:48,476 --> 00:01:54,576
Arisan. Try it on devnet today: the app and the Android APK are linked on screen.

